msgid "HIRING_FORM_VERIFIED"
msgstr "The original employee-hiring form and its displayed stat schema have been recovered from the VB6 executable."

msgid "APPLICANT_ROSTER_PENDING"
msgstr "Applicant source names and values are still being decoded; the roster algorithm is recovered, and no placeholder candidates are invented in this build."

msgid "APPLICANT_REFRESH_EVIDENCE"
msgstr "The original form rebuilds its five-slot roster when opened. Its random selection rule is recovered; source records remain pending."

msgid "APPLICANT_COUNT"
msgstr "Applicants: {0}"

msgid "HIRING_ACTION_PENDING"
msgstr "Hire becomes active once the original applicant generation and contract behavior are decoded."

msgid "M4_OFFICE_NOTE"
msgstr "Milestone 4 opens the verified employee-hiring form. Game development remains the next major reconstruction boundary."

msgid "M4_BOUNDARY"
msgstr "Milestone 4 reconstructs the hiring UI and the PC game's employee stat model. Candidate generation and the actual contract transaction are intentionally still blocked until recovered from the original."

msgid "M5_RECRUITMENT_RULES"
msgstr "Recovered roster rule: 5 applicant slots. Source records whose original gate/flag test passes then face a 1-in-4 random acceptance test per scan until the roster is filled."

msgid "M5_HIRE_RULES"
msgstr "Recovered hire rule: hiring is rejected when funds are below the selected contract fee; a successful hire copies that applicant into the employee roster and charges the contract fee."

msgid "M5_DATABASE_PENDING"
msgstr "The source employee database and its eligibility field are still being decoded, so real applicant identities and stats remain disabled rather than fabricated."

msgid "M5_OFFICE_NOTE"
msgstr "Milestone 5 recovers the hiring transaction and the 5-slot roster-selection algorithm. The source employee database is the next recruitment boundary."

msgid "M5_BOUNDARY"
msgstr "Milestone 5 has decoded the roster shape, random acceptance test, affordability check, employee-copy helper, and contract-fee charge. Real applicants remain blocked until their source database is recovered."

